================================================================================
HABIT & TASK TRACKER - MASTER FEATURE MAP & ROADMAP
================================================================================

1. CORE ARCHITECTURE & TECH STACK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Framework: Python + Flet (ft.run) with decoupled SQLite database (backend.py / tasks.db).
- Target Platforms: Desktop (Windows/Linux/macOS) first, followed by Mobile (Android/iOS).
- Distribution Model: Anki-style open/free desktop model (no paywall on PC); optional mobile/pro features later.
- First-Run Experience: High-clarity onboarding screen + strong store/app keywords.
- Aesthetic Direction: Clean, functional, dark-mode-first UI during development; custom handcrafted skins (e.g., Y2K hardware faceplates) designed externally later after core app is complete.

2. UI & DYNAMIC THEME ENGINE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Default Theme: Dark mode ("Nordic Pine" / deep dark-gray surface #121212) with high-contrast readable text.
- Custom Theme Studio: Live preview modal with curated presets, target-layer selector (Accent, Background, Card Surface, Box/Shelf), RGB sliders, hex code input, and persistent SQLite storage.
- Time Format Toggle: Global 24-hour (14:30) and 12-hour AM/PM (2:30 PM) display setting.

3. NAVIGATION & PAGE BREAKDOWN
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[Page 1] Schedule & Today (Active Tasks View)
  - Defaults to Today's tasks on boot.
  - Sub-views: Day, Week, and Month views with scroll-wheel, swipe, and button navigation.
  - Day View: Daily completion progress bar at top, task cards with checkboxes, inline unit logging banner, notes, reminder badges, and expandable inline edit/delete drawer.
  - Week View: Vertical top-to-bottom 7-day stack (Mon-Sun) with weekly momentum progress bar at the top (prevents text cutoff on narrow PC windows and mobile screens).
  - Month View: Calendar grid clearly showing scheduled tasks and completion counts per day; clicking a day jumps directly into that Day view.
  - Quick-Add Shortcut: '+' button inside calendar views to create tasks pre-scheduled for the active date.

[Page 2] Add Task / Habit Form
  - Defaults recurrence to "Once" for fast one-off task entry.
  - Supports Recurring Habits: Weekly/Daily (interactive day balls + All-7 toggle), Monthly/Yearly (12-month grid), and Every-X-Days custom intervals.
  - Quantifiable Units: Optional unit tracking (kg, lb, km, sets, reps, mins, hours, pages, or custom unit) for recurring habits.
  - Restart/Copy Past Habit: Dropdown to auto-fill settings from any existing habit and link history.
  - Reminders & End Dates: Apple-alarm-style time wheel picker and optional end-date/duration presets.

[Page 3] Backlog Queue
  - Unscheduled task list for ideas/tasks without a target date yet.
  - One-click scheduling buttons (Today, Tomorrow, or date picker) to move items onto the active schedule.
  - QoL: Ability to mark backlog tasks completed directly inside the backlog view, plus inline edit & delete.

[Page 4] Habits & Data Analytics
  - Scope Filter: Inspect Everything (Global), an Individual Habit, or a Category, plus a Custom Date Range Inspector (From / To).
  - Streak & Consistency Cards: Current Streak, Best Streak, Completion Rate %, and Completed vs. Missed counts.
  - Anki/GitHub-Style Contribution Heatmap: Horizontal grid scaling from dark surface up to bright neon accent; marks unscheduled days with subtle dots on non-daily habits.
  - Unit Progression Charts: SVG Line and Pillar charts with Running Average, Weekly Session Average, and Goal Benchmark lines.
  - Multi-Goal Setting: Set Max/Peak, Weekly Average, or Overall Average goals with optional target deadlines and achievement tracking.

[Page 5] All Database Tasks
  - Master searchable and category-filterable list of all tasks/habits in SQLite.
  - Inline edit drawer for modifying any task property.
  - Batch Selection Mode: Multi-select checkboxes with "Are you sure?" confirmation safeguard for bulk deletion.

4. INTERACTION & UX (PC & MOBILE)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- PC Keyboard-Driven Speed:
  - Global number keys (1-5) to switch main tabs instantly.
  - Left/Right arrow keys to shift dates; 'T' to snap to Today.
  - Up/Down arrow keys to highlight tasks and Enter/Space to toggle completion.
  - Escape key to close popups/drawers; typing-state lock so shortcuts never fire while typing in text fields.
- Mobile Responsiveness & Touch:
  - Adaptive layout for narrow phone viewports (thumb-friendly bottom navigation bar, stacked headers, full-width cards).
  - Horizontal swipe gestures for date navigation and support for external mobile keyboards.

5. DOPAMINE LOOP & REMINDERS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Visual Stimulation: Instant checkmark fills, progress bar transitions, completion flash/pulse animations, and Goal Achievement celebration feedback when hitting unit targets.
- Audio Cues: Crisp, satisfying sound effects on task completion and goal milestones (toggleable in Settings).
- Haptics: Subtle device vibration triggers on mobile builds.
- Notifications: Native desktop notifications (Windows/Linux) via Python helper libraries, syncing with local notifications on mobile.

